   "text": {
    "L1": "Kabir is always inventing something. His curiosity makes him keep trying.",
    "L2": "The machine failed, but that did not mean Kabir had failed.",
    "L3": "The failure showed him what was wrong, so he could improve the machine.",
    "L4": "First, Kabir started building a machine to fold rotis.",
    "L5": "While he was building it, Mummy walked in. The machine shook and threw a roti onto the fan.",
    "L6": "Everyone laughed, but the narrator sounded amused, fond, and a little proud of Kabir.",
    "L7": "For an action already in progress, use was or were plus the verb ending in -ing.",
    "L8": "Use the simple past for the action that interrupts it: Kabir was building when Mummy walked in.",
    "L9": "Now put the story events in the order they happened."
   },
